# 8. Limitation Analysis

The evaluation identified the following limitations.

## Semantic Drift

Highly paraphrased legal questions may retrieve procedurally related articles instead of conceptually related constitutional provisions.

## Embedding Model Limitations

Although multilingual-e5-base supports multiple languages, it is not specifically trained on Ethiopian legal texts.

## Query Template Dependency

The improved retrieval performance depends on template-based query alignment. Any future schema changes require updating the query template.

## Legal Corpus Coverage

Only the FDRE Constitution is indexed. Other Ethiopian legal documents are not yet included.

## Infrastructure

The local Qdrant deployment is memory-based and may require scaling for larger legal collections.

---

# 9. Recommended Configuration

The following configuration achieved the best retrieval performance.

| Component | Recommended Configuration |
|-----------|---------------------------|
| Embedding Model | intfloat/multilingual-e5-base |
| Vector Database | Qdrant (Cosine Similarity) |
| Query Strategy | Template-Based Query Alignment |
| Re-ranking | Continuous Title Boost |
| Top-K | 3 |
| Safe Fallback | Hard Reject + Similarity Threshold |

